# wasm-pack emits the binary here; commit the JS + .d.ts glue, ignore the built .wasm (mirrors the
# napi crate's `*.node` ignore — SMA-427).
#
# NOTE: `wasm-pack build --out-dir .` CLEANS this dir each run — it overwrites this file with a bare
# `*` and DELETES the hand-written package.json (even with --no-pack). We intend the opposite: commit
# the glue + package.json, ignore only the binary. Phase 2's moon build/test reruns wasm-pack, so it
# MUST re-assert this file and package.json afterward (the committed glue + package.json are what the
# `@paigasus/wasm` file: link resolves). Re-check both after any rebuild.
*.wasm
